          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A febrile patient in the emergency department has a qSOFA score of 2. Which of t</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A febrile patient in the emergency department has a qSOFA score of 2. Which of the following clinical findings is NOT one of the three qSOFA parameters?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Respiratory rate of 24 breaths per minute</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Respiratory rate ≥22 is one of the three qSOFA parameters. A rate of 24 would contribute 1 point to the score.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Altered mentation</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Altered mentation (any reduction in Glasgow Coma Scale from baseline) is one of the three qSOFA parameters, contributing 1 point.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Temperature of 39.5°C</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Temperature is deliberately excluded from qSOFA. The score uses only three bedside data points — respiratory rate ≥22, altered mentation, and systolic blood pressure ≤100 mmHg — because it identifies organ dysfunction risk, not the presence of infection itself.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Systolic blood pressure of 95 mmHg</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Systolic blood pressure ≤100 mmHg is one of the three qSOFA parameters, contributing 1 point to the score.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "Review the qSOFA criteria: the score uses exactly three bedside data points — respiratory rate ≥22, altered mentation, and systolic blood pressure ≤100 mmHg. Temperature is not included. A score of 2 or more triggers urgent sepsis assessment."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. qSOFA deliberately uses only three bedside parameters — respiratory rate, mentation, and blood pressure — to flag organ dysfunction risk. Temperature, though clinically important, is not part of the qSOFA score."
                }
              ],
